From 4802a495a7a5357544ec2ca60c0cee4484e75c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(entities): bridge authoritative native picking hitboxes

Keep native picking boxes, Java interaction proxies and negotiated client snapshots above the shared metadata state. Preserve alias click coordinates, connection lifetimes and ordinary Java interaction fallback.

The marker translation leaves source invisibility, equipment and entity
identity independent. Java marker dimensions are zero rather than the
native .005 clamp, and marker state suppresses picking and building
obstruction. The accepted native proxy add-on can reconstruct the proved
collapsed-box name anchor from marker state. Arbitrary armor-stand sizes
still require an explicit native metadata bridge.

Retain metadata118 picking boxes independently from physical dimensions53/54.
Target Bedrock 1.26.51.1/build51061372/protocol2193 decoder14337dc20 reads
FloatTag Min/Max/Pivot components, defaults missing or wrong types to zero,
sorts endpoints and recenters extents around actor position plus pivot.
Eight original parser/lookup/translation controls establish those CPU
operations; picker1435282e0 consumes the per-part list before physical
fallback. Do not infer scaling, radius inflation or arbitrary pick height.

Expose general nonphysical Java Interaction targets for each retained part,
refresh them on sparse metadata/position changes and remove aliases with
actor lifetime. Resolve interactions back to the authoritative owner while
preserving the target-relative click position. Negotiate exact rectangular
part dimensions separately for clients that support both native actor and
picking capabilities; ordinary Java retains enclosing Interaction widths.
Invalid or missing data never creates a guessed native picking rectangle.

Ordinary Java entity hits are relative to the displayed entity base, not
Bedrock's actor origin. Convert them through javaPosition so boats and
players do not add their hull/eye offsets to outgoing world hits.
Protocol 2225 captures from native 1.26.60.5 and BDS 1.26.60.6 show a boat
hit at Y64.555, while the old Java path reports Y64.93747. Regression tests cover boat movement, player origins, and proxy aliases.

Native 1.26.60.5 protocol2225 captures include the picked world position
in actor attacks. Java's attack packet omits that position, so an optional
negotiated payload replaces it atomically for supporting frontends.
Validate the published owner and lifetime, including multipart aliases,
before forwarding the actual pick through the shared attack writer.
Keep ordinary Java attacks available when that capability is absent.
No pending hit survives to another attack, target, or actor lifetime.

Matching 1.26.60.5 boat top/front/side hits and armor-stand front/side
hits establish physical fallback picking as the scaled collision box
expanded by 0.1 blocks on each face. Java's vanilla hull instead changes
the selected plane. Reuse the nonphysical picking proxies when the native
geometry bridge is negotiated, retain authored hitboxes as the first
choice, and leave physical dimensions and ordinary Java fallback intact.
Replay existing actors when the capability arrives after their spawn.

Bedrock 1.26.60.5 / protocol2225 and BDS1.26.60.6 native controls
admit block centers inside 5.7 blocks and reject centers outside that
radius, independently of the stone or fence hit surface and diagonal
approach. Send the native maximum range to Java at join and after mode
changes; abilities alone leave Java at 4.5 block and 3 entity reach.
Native entity candidates use 3 blocks in Survival and 5.7 in Creative.

Separate reach admission from the physical fallback's 0.1 surface pad.
Settled native armor-stand attacks reach the padded face at 2.89 blocks,
but 2.91 only swings, for empty hand and sword. Creative admits 5.6,
but 5.61 only swings. Version the picking channel so a frontend never
interprets the old surface-only snapshot as physical reach metadata.
Authored boxes retain zero padding and their existing geometry.

Advertise the negotiated attack capability after the play join even in
an empty world. The frontend uses that same v2 negotiation to enable
block-center admission; older proxy cores keep their original picker.
